Leave DRM objects leased to another program out of the compositor's modesets

A connector marked for lease is handed to another program to drive, but every
mutter update that contains a mode set first clears CRTC_ID on every connector
of the card, the leased one included, without disabling that connector's CRTC.
The result is an enabled CRTC with nothing attached, which the kernel refuses
with "enabled/connectors mismatch", and since an atomic commit is all or
nothing, the part of the same request that would light the compositor's own
screens is refused with it. Waking a screen from sleep is such a request, so
once the leased connector is lit, the desktop cannot come back from a blank
until a hotplug makes mutter rebuild its state.

Track the objects handed to each lessee and leave them alone when clearing the
card, so that mutter's requests describe only what it still owns.

Applies to mutter 50.1.

